%S A204520 0,1,2,3,7,9,18,47,123,161,322,843,2207,2889,5778,15127,39603,51841,
%T A204520 103682,271443,710647,930249,1860498,4870847,12752043,16692641,
%U A204520 33385282,87403803,228826127,299537289,599074578,1568397607,4106118243,5374978561,10749957122
%N A204520 Numbers k such that floor(k^2 / 5) is a square.
%C A204520 Also: Numbers whose square, with its last base-5 digit dropped, is again a square. (For the three initial terms whose squares have only one digit in base 5, it is then understood that this yields zero.)
%C A204520 The g.f. in the Formula section (originally empirical) is correct: floor(a^2/5) = b^2 iff 0 <= a^2 - 5*b^2 <= 4, i.e., a^2 - 5*b^2 is 0, 1 or 4, since squares are 0, 1 or 4 mod 5. Multiplication of a + b*sqrt(5) by 9 + 4*sqrt(5) maps solutions to solutions and, for a >= 36, preserves their order; with a direct check of the terms below 36 this gives a(n) = 18*a(n-4) - a(n-8) for n >= 10, and hence the g.f. - _Zachary Kleckner_, Nov 11 2026
%H A204520 Zachary Kleckner, <a href="/A204520/b204520.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1000</a>
%H A204520 <a href="/index/Rec#order_08">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (0,0,0,18,0,0,0,-1).
%F A204520 a(n) = sqrt(A055812(n)).
%F A204520 G.f.: -x^2*(x+1)*(3*x^6 + 4*x^5 + 14*x^4 - 5*x^3 - 2*x^2 - x-1) / ((x^4 - 4*x^2 - 1)*(x^4 + 4*x^2 - 1)). - _Colin Barker_, Sep 15 2014
%F A204520 a(n) = 18*a(n-4) - a(n-8) for n >= 10. - _Zachary Kleckner_, Nov 11 2026
%F A204520 a(4*k+2) = L(6*k)/2, a(4*k+3) = L(6*k), a(4*k+4) = L(6*k+2), a(4*k+5) = L(6*k+4), where L = A000032. - _Jianing Song_, Nov 12 2026
%t A204520 Select[Range[0,5*10^6],IntegerQ[Sqrt[Floor[#^2/5]]]&] (* The program generates the first 24 terms of the sequence. *) (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Jul 15 2025 *)
%o A204520 (PARI) b=5;for(n=0,2e9,issquare(n^2\b) && print1(n","))
%Y A204520 Cf. A055812, A204521.
%Y A204520 Cf. A031149, A055812, A204502, A204514, A204516, A204518 and A004275, A001075, A001541 for the analog in bases 10,...,6 and 4, 3, 2.
%K A204520 nonn,easy,changed
%O A204520 1,3
%A A204520 _M. F. Hasler_, Jan 15 2012
